<script>
  import { samples } from "$sources";
  let live = $state(true);
</script>

<title>NaN and Infinity</title>

<p><a href="/">← All pages</a></p>
<h1>NaN and Infinity</h1>
<p>A known divergence. Rust renders these values directly, but the handoff payload is JSON, which has no NaN or Infinity, so they reach the browser as <code>null</code>. Toggle the region twice to see the browser's version.</p>
<button id="toggle" onclick={() => live = !live}>Toggle the live region</button>
<DataSource source={samples} load="server" let:data>
  {#if live}
  <dl id="out">
    <dt>NaN</dt><dd id="nan">{data.notANumber}</dd>
    <dt>Infinity</dt><dd id="inf">{data.infinite}</dd>
  </dl>
  {/if}
</DataSource>

<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 44rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
</style>
